  "settingsAbout": "About COROC",
  "aboutVersion": "Version",
  "aboutPrivacy": "Your clients' data lives encrypted on your company's server; this device only keeps the session in the system's secure storage.",
  "helpSubtitle": "Short guides to what you can do in COROC today.",
  "helpSearch": "Search help",
  "helpNoResults": "No topics match that word.",
  "helpFooter": "COROC {version} · Personal loans",
  "helpLoginTitle": "Signing in and protecting your account",
  "helpLoginBody": "To sign in you need your company code, your username and your password. The Owner must turn on two-step verification with an authenticator app; other users can turn it on in Settings › Security. After several failed attempts the account is locked for a period that grows with each lockout. If you forgot your password, use \"Forgot your password?\" to get a link valid for 30 minutes.",
  "helpNewClientTitle": "Adding a client with their first loan",
  "helpNewClientBody": "Use \"New client\". The wizard has three steps: client details (name, WhatsApp mobile and, optionally, ID, email and co-signer), loan terms with a live preview, and consents. If the mobile number or ID already exists, COROC warns you before creating a duplicate. When you finish, it assigns the client number and contract and builds the payment schedule and client folder.",
  "helpMethodsTitle": "Simple interest or fixed installment",
  "helpMethodsBody": "Simple interest: the rate is a percentage of principal for the whole term; for example, 1,000 at 20% over 30 installments totals 1,200, i.e. 40 per installment. Fixed installment (amortized): the rate is per payment period and every installment is the same; early ones carry more interest and later ones more principal. Either way, the preview shows the installment, total, profit and effective annual rate before you save.",
  "helpRateCapTitle": "Legal rate caps and usury",
  "helpRateCapBody": "COROC converts any rate to an effective annual rate and compares it with the cap in force on the disbursement date. In Colombia the cap is the usury rate certified by the Financial Superintendence: record it every month in Settings › Legal rate caps. If a rate exceeds it, the loan isn't saved and the preview offers the highest allowed rate. Late fees can't exceed the cap either.",
  "helpScheduleTitle": "The payment schedule",
  "helpScheduleBody": "On the client page, the \"Payment schedule\" tab lists every installment with its date, principal, interest, amount paid, payment date, status, receipts and balance afterwards. Holidays and non-collection days are skipped automatically. Everything is rebuilt from the activity, so it always matches the receipts.",
  "helpPaymentsTitle": "Recording a payment",
  "helpPaymentsBody": "Use \"Record payment\" from the client page or Today's collections. Before confirming you'll see how it applies: first to late fees, then to the oldest installment. You can pay part of an installment or several at once. Confirming issues the thank-you receipt with its number and verification code. If the connection drops and you retry, the payment is not duplicated.",
  "helpReversalTitle": "Reversing a payment",
  "helpReversalBody": "Payments are never deleted; they are reversed. In the \"Activity\" tab, pick the payment, enter a reason and confirm. The receipt is voided, the schedule is recalculated, and the action is logged in the audit trail with its author. Only the Owner and Administrators can reverse.",
  "helpDashboardTitle": "Reading the dashboard",
  "helpDashboardBody": "Capital out is the outstanding principal of active loans. Expected today adds installments due today plus anything overdue. Total receivable includes principal, agreed interest and late fees. The aging card groups balances into current, 1–7, 8–30 and over 30 days past due. Figures update live when someone records a payment. If you use several currencies, each is shown separately.",
  "helpRolesTitle": "Roles and permissions",
  "helpRolesBody": "Owner: everything, including billing and restoring backups. Administrator: everything else. Collector: sees only assigned clients and records payments; the database itself prevents access to others. Auditor: read-only. Every denied access is logged in the audit trail.",
  "helpSecurityTitle": "Device security",
  "helpSecurityBody": "The app locks after the idle time you choose in Settings and unlocks with fingerprint, face or the device PIN. When you switch apps, the content is hidden. COROC keeps no client data on your phone or computer, only the session, encrypted in the system's secure storage. In Settings › Security you can see and sign out other devices.",
  "helpLanguageTitle": "Languages",
  "helpLanguageBody": "COROC works in Spanish, Brazilian Portuguese and English. Change the language in Settings › Preferences or on the sign-in screen; it takes effect immediately. Each client has their own language for receipts and messages, regardless of the app user's language. Amounts always use their currency's format.",
  "helpShortcutsTitle": "Keyboard shortcuts",
  "helpShortcutsBody": "On desktop: Ctrl + K (⌘ + K on Mac) opens client search and Ctrl + N (⌘ + N) starts a new client. Tab moves between fields and Enter confirms dialogs.",
