  "restoreDoneBody": "The backup data and documents are now in the company. Other users with the app open will see the changes when they refresh.",
  "helpDocumentsTitle": "Documents and PDF receipts",
  "helpDocumentsBody": "COROC generates automatically, in the client's language: the contract and payment plan when the loan is created (with a new version whenever it changes), the \"Thank you for your payment\" receipt with its verification QR code after every payment, the statement every month and when the loan closes, and the payoff letter when the balance reaches zero. A reversal never deletes the receipt: a VOID-stamped version is issued. Documents are never overwritten; Details shows their versions and SHA-256 fingerprint. All files are stored encrypted on the server and open through links that expire in minutes.",
  "helpFolderTitle": "COROC folder",
  "helpFolderBody": "The COROC folder is a copy of the whole repository on your device: one folder per client (\"First Last - Code\", without accents so it works on every system and cloud) and, inside, one per contract with \"01 Contract and payment plan\", \"02 Received receipts\", \"03 Issued receipts\", \"04 Statements\" and \"05 Other documents\". There are also _Unassigned, _Inbox, _Reports and _Backups. It updates itself while the app is open and, if a client changes name, the folder is renamed without losing files. On desktop, photos and PDFs you drop in _Inbox or in a client folder go to the review inbox on their own; other files are offered for import. COROC never deletes your other files. On Android it only uses the folder you choose; on iOS you will find it in Files.",
  "helpReportsTitle": "Reports",
  "helpReportsBody": "In Reports you generate the total or per-collector portfolio, collections by period, aging, paid-off loans and profit, cash flow projection, the ledger and the message log, as PDF, XLSX or CSV and in Spanish, Portuguese or English. Each report shows the cut-off date and filters and uses a single currency: COROC never adds different currencies. They are kept in _Reports. Collectors cannot generate company-wide reports.",
  "helpBackupTitle": "Backup and restore",
  "helpBackupBody": "\"Create backup\" produces a .coroc file with all company data and documents, encrypted with AES-256 and the password you choose (COROC does not store it). It includes a manifest with the SHA-256 fingerprint of every file. It is built on the server while you keep working, can be cancelled, and the download resumes if interrupted; it is kept in _Backups and you can save it elsewhere. Only the Owner can restore: COROC checks integrity and version, shows how much will be restored and asks you to type the company name. The restore is atomic: if anything fails, nothing changes. Users in the backup must turn on two-step verification again.",
